{"term":"fountain","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d49bd3c49be307cc79","definition":"A natural source of water; a spring.","example":"A little fountaine became a riuer, and there was light, & the Sunne, and much water: this riuer is Eſther, whō the King married and made Queene.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["fount","syke","wellspring"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air fountain","chain fountain","drinking fountain","fire fountain","fountain apple moss","fountain chair","fountain code","Fountaindale","fountain drink","fountaineer","fountain effect","fountaingrass","fountainhead","Fountain Hills","fountain lamp","fountainless","fountainlet","fountainlike","fountain of youth","fountainous","fountain pen","fountain pressure","Fountains Earth","fountain shell","fountain water","fountainwise","Heron's fountain","ice fountain","ink fountain","kugel fountain"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6476618a97d49967b3","definition":"An artificial, usually ornamental, water feature (usually in a garden or public place) consisting of one or more streams of water originating from a statue or other structure.","example":"His house is right beside that fountain on Street 15.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air fountain","chain fountain","drinking fountain","fire fountain","fountain apple moss","fountain chair","fountain code","Fountaindale","fountain drink","fountaineer","fountain effect","fountaingrass","fountainhead","Fountain Hills","fountain lamp","fountainless","fountainlet","fountainlike","fountain of youth","fountainous","fountain pen","fountain pressure","Fountains Earth","fountain shell","fountain water","fountainwise","Heron's fountain","ice fountain","ink fountain","kugel fountain"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaik